 "id": "2026-11-13-hormuz-pipeline-two-fronts",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Saudi Arabia's oil route around Hormuz just came under fire. What does that mean?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "First, the strait itself. Iran's Revolutionary Guards say two supertankers were disabled by explosions, after ignoring warnings on what Tehran calls an unauthorised route. Iran's army reported two more tankers hit by mines. Reuters could not verify the Iranian account."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Then Yemen's Houthis claimed strikes on a pumping station of Saudi Arabia's East-West pipeline, an oil site in Yanbu, and an Aramco building in Riyadh. Saudi Arabia did not confirm. Reuters says the pipeline carries about four million barrels a day around Hormuz."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Markets reacted. Brent crude rose three point three percent on Thursday, to almost ninety-six dollars a barrel. And President Trump now says the U.S. no longer needs a deal with Iran, while the U.S. blockade of Iranian ports goes on."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will the Strait of Hormuz reopen before the new year? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
